o work as a  team raptors are back animals and young  ones grow at a fast pace and so they  need to learn how to run around and hunt  to survive in the wild  baby blue as i would like to call her  also has the same stripes as her parent  which means that baby blue might also be  capable of empathy as her parent  we then see owen brady  reunited with blue doing that hand  gesture trying to make her remember him  since they would have been apart for  quite a while since fallen kingdom owen  then talks to claire about blue being  safe in the remote forested region else  they would never be together again which  means that blue is on some sort of  reserve devoid of human population else  a human animal conflict would result in  a hunt for her and that wouldn't be safe  for her either for the baby we then jump  into the next clip and it's a mosasaurus  attacking a fishing vessel trying to  tuck away a fish catch from the boat we  hear them say in the background that  releasing the dinos from lockwood  mansion proved to be an ecological  disaster  and that the diners are wreaking havoc  on the food chain they become the alpha  predators and their place in the world  is chaos we then see the same clip of  the t-rex in the movie drive-in as in  the prologue the same one from the  prologue a few months back this proves  the same point that the dinosaurs don't  really have a place in the modern world  so the next set of clips shows us ellie  sadler and alan grant in a similar  backdrop from the first jurassic movie  it's the first time  they were seen together in the franchise  since jurassic park 3. we see the  dinosaur man in his excavation site with  which is kind of like a throwback from  the first movie where alan grant and  ellie are working together on digging up  fossils and they were recruited by john  hammond to visit his park full of  real-life dinos but here in the scene it  was ellie that calls gran for a mission  that needs his expertise which is kind  of probab